      "writtenOn": "2021-03-10T16:16:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there a better way to get the list of UIDs to which we should allow debug access?",
      "revId": "c14ba104c8b0715ad70d507ee2023fbeea43d0fd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1cfb6565_c7a1c464",
        "filename": "virtmanager/src/aidl.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 32,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042276
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-10T17:41:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This would be needed if different UIDs could reach the service.  But since you\u0027ll have to allow only shell to find this service in SELinux anyway, wouldn\u0027t it be enough?",
      "parentUuid": "768742fa_6f5e5bd6",
      "revId": "c14ba104c8b0715ad70d507ee2023fbeea43d0fd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fece851a_762b5db6",
        "filename": "virtmanager/src/aidl.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 32,
      "author": {
        "id": 1059815
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-10T18:19:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think there is a better way. The UIDs are hardcoded in frameworks/base/core/java/android/os/Process.java and those constants used in various services (cs/Process.SHELL_UID). Is there Rust FFI for Java to export the constants from the Process class?",
      "parentUuid": "1cfb6565_c7a1c464",
      "revId": "c14ba104c8b0715ad70d507ee2023fbeea43d0fd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "306ee1e5_8b12933e",
        "filename": "virtmanager/src/aidl.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 32,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-11T04:23:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The proper way is to define a permission, give shell UID the permission, and check if the calling UID has the permission.\n\nBut it looks like rust binder doesn\u0027t have checkPermission. https://source.corp.google.com/android/frameworks/native/libs/binder/include/binder/PermissionController.h;rcl\u003dcb046678fda5ae2d926911611ae932fefab6e519;l\u003d48\n\nSo, **for now**, you might have to directly check the UID instead. The source of truth is here: system/core/libcutils/include/private/android_filesystem_config.h, but I don\u0027t know how you can import that into rust.\n\nEventually, this should be fixed, because you will have to check whether the calling process (app) has a permission to create a VM. We will have to define a permission like android.permission.CREATE_VM or similar. You won\u0027t be able to use UID there.",
      "parentUuid": "fece851a_762b5db6",
      "revId": "c14ba104c8b0715ad70d507ee2023fbeea43d0fd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
