        "id": 1042276
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-10T17:41:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For my education, is VmInstance hold remotely by the client? I wonder how the reference counting works remotely.  Is it done through IVirtualMachine with some binder magic? Is the VirtualMachine object still hold by the service once returned from VirtManager::startVm? Consider adding some comment somewhere.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 108,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 108,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "c14ba104c8b0715ad70d507ee2023fbeea43d0fd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5c20e2da_e473ac8f",
        "filename": "virtmanager/src/aidl.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 108,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-11T15:57:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, Binder handles reference counting between processes. And then within this process, the Binder library holds a `VirtualMachine`, which in turn holds a strong reference to `VmInstance`. Added a comment.",
      "parentUuid": "fdf69821_2c282022",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 108,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 108,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "c14ba104c8b0715ad70d507ee2023fbeea43d0fd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
